The  kernel interface adds compilation of filter programs sent to
a device.  Instead of being interpreted for every  packet,  these
filter programs are compiled into native code and the code is be‐
ing executed for every packet.  The implementation of is based on
the  library,  or for short.  The library supports multiple plat‐
forms including AMD‐x86 64 ARM 32 (ARM‐v5, ARM‐v7 and Thumb2  in‐
struction  sets) Intel‐x86 32 MIPS 32 (III, R1) MIPS 64 (III, R1)
PowerPC 32 PowerPC 64 SPARC 32 supports all architectures  listed
above.   is  also  available as a module in modular kernels.  The
following sysctl is available when is enabled: Toggle compilation
of new filter programs.  Changing a value of this sysctl  doesn’t
